# 🧠 14. CONSTRAINTS MATTER

Suppose:

```text
n ≤ 20
```

An:

$$
O(2^n)
$$

solution might be possible.

But if:

```text
n ≤ 10^5
```

then:

$$
O(2^n)
$$

is impossible.

### Rough placement rule:

|     n | Usually consider            |
| ----: | --------------------------- |
|  ≤ 10 | Brute force / Backtracking  |
|  ≤ 20 | Bitmask / Backtracking / DP |
| ≤ 10³ | O(n²) may work              |
| ≤ 10⁵ | O(n log n) / O(n)           |
| ≤ 10⁶ | Usually O(n)                |

Not absolute—but a useful first filter.

